# Clean research model for LDR deep-research (NO RS2 prompt — would derail search).
# This model ONLY searches and summarizes web pages. All reasoning/judgment lives in
# rs2-analyst (qwen3.6:35b-a3b), which is unchanged — do not "simplify" by pointing
# deep_research at the analyst: its baked RS2 prompt derails LDR's research prompts.
#
# FROM qwen3:14b (was qwen3.6:35b-a3b) — 2026-08-04, after 115 of 250 tickers shipped
# ollama error text as their research brief. The 35b weights are 22,960 MiB on a
# 24,576 MiB card: ~790MB of headroom, measured. That is fine on a quiet box (verified
# loading twice, incl. a full 8192-ctx request) but not during a run, where the real
# failure chain is:
#     llama-server GPU discovery watchdog timed out ("context deadline exceeded")
#     unable to refresh free memory, using old values
#     system memory total="11.8 GiB" free="2.3 GiB"     <- box thrashing
#     gpu memory available="22.3 GiB" free="22.8 GiB"   <- STALE reading
#     alloc_tensor_range: failed to allocate CUDA0 buffer of size 22746292736
#   -> then the CPU projector retry wants ~23GB against 2.3GB free RAM and dies.
# With <1GB of margin a single stale reading is fatal. num_gpu is NOT the lever: 42 and
# 99 both load 100% GPU (ollama ps confirms) and both leave ~790MB free.
# qwen3:14b is 9.3GB -> ~15GB headroom, which survives a stale reading, and it loads
# faster so it adds less RAM pressure at the moment discovery is most likely to time out.
FROM qwen3:14b
PARAMETER num_gpu 99
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER temperature 0.3
